package mcpserver

const RuntimeUserDecisionInstructions = `Every CODEX_REQUEST requires an explicit user answer from the current conversation. Read operation_get(include=RUNTIME_REQUESTS) for its exact persisted runtimeRequestId before displaying Codex's original question and original options. Keep explanation separate; do not preselect, recommend, infer from AGENTS.md/Project Context/history, or author/translate/supplement the answer. A notification is not user consent. Until the user answers, do not submit a UserDecision, runtime response, StartTurn or replacement Run. A drafted answer must be shown and its exact final text explicitly confirmed before submission.
Bind each answer to one exact request; latest or ordering is never authority, and one ambiguous yes cannot consume multiple requests. runtime_request_user_decision_prepare_hash is a pure read for the canonical checksum; it records nothing and grants no consent. Only runtime_request_user_decision_submit records the exact user-selected option/raw text with stable submissionRequestId and payloadSHA256. runtime_request_respond for CODEX_REQUEST requires the durable UserDecision reference, never raw model-authored response JSON. RUNTIME_APPROVAL remains a separate permission admission and cannot consume an engineering question.
RESPOND continues the same operation within its frozen revision and RuntimeWorkset; it grants no expanded scope. STOP_AND_REVISE and CANCEL_OPERATION use authoritative cancellation, never a continue answer. A successor needs its own existing formal confirmation after quiescence. For RESPONSE_DISPOSITION_UNKNOWN say exactly: 你的回答已经记录。Codex 可能已经收到该回答，但当前协议无法确认。Dev Bridge 不会自动重发。 Even if the user says resend, do not call runtime_request_respond or submit another decision. Offer only CONTINUE_WAITING, CANCEL_OPERATION, STOP_AND_REVISE via runtime_request_recovery; safe redispatch requires internal exact pending evidence. UNKNOWN means the answer is recorded but backend consumption is unconfirmed: do not ask again, overwrite, blindly resend, or start a replacement. Read exact recovery facts. Wakeup failure, ALREADY_ATTEMPTED and unconfirmed host visibility never answer, cancel or duplicate the request. Waiting requests remain visible through workspace/operation reads; refresh is read-only. Runtime-question conversation responses use this narrow explicit-user path and do not bypass formal Task/Review/Execution confirmations. This exact-question wakeup contract is independent of file-mode confirmation continuation.`
